// Stand-in for the now-UNCONDITIONAL uidialogs.cla manifest entry
// (runtime-ir-bake Task 2: the from-source splice moved to the full lane
// superset) in this fake runtime-module directory (Task 4's
// inclusion-machinery test, internal/lowlevel/rtinc_test.go). Deliberately
// empty, same reason as this directory's core.cla/str.cla/text.cla/
// list.cla/map.cla stand-ins: this directory exercises expand's
// declare-before-use splicing machinery, not uidialogs.cla's real content --
// the real module lives at runtime/clarus/uidialogs.cla. driveManifestSplice
// now always adds "uidialogs.cla" to neededMods regardless of program shape,
// so --rtdir testdata/rtinc/rt needs SOME file by that name (an
// empty/decl-less file pushes main.cla's own "-1 head" empty-file
// sentinel, already handled) or TestRtInc's IncludesRuntimeModule/
// NoInclusionWithoutUsage subtests fail with "runtime module uidialogs.cla
// not found" before ever reaching the assertions they actually care
// about.
